{
  "case_id": "2021-21-463",
  "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "S. B. 8 does not allow state offcials to bring criminal prosecutions or civil actions to enforce the law but instead directs enforcement through \u201cprivate civil actions\u201d culminating in injunctions and statutory damages awards against those who perform or assist with prohibited abortions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The petitioners are abortion providers who sought pre-enforcement review of S. B. 8 in federal court based on the allegation that S. B. 8 violates the Federal Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The public-offcial defendants moved to dismiss the complaint citing, among other things, the doctrine of sovereign immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Firearms Policy Coalition",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Erik S. Jaffe fled a brief of amicus curiae for the Firearms Policy Coalition urging reversal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We conclude that such an action is permissible against some of the named defendants but not others."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0000-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And given the statute's approaching effective date, they asked us to rule within two days. The Court took up the application and, in the abbreviated time available for review, concluded that the petitioners' submission failed to identify a basis in existing law suffcient to justify disturbing the Court of Appeals' decision denying injunctive relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the end, the petitioners say, they intend to seek an order enjoining all state-court clerks from docketing S. B. 8 cases and all state-court judges from hearing them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Generally, States are immune from suit under the terms of the Eleventh Amendment and the doctrine of sovereign immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Accordingly, we hold that sovereign immunity does not bar the petitioners' suit against these named defendants at the motion to dismiss stage."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has never recognized an unqualifed right to pre-enforcement review of constitutional claims in federal court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would reverse in full the District Court's denial of respondents' motions to dismiss and remand with instructions to dismiss the case for lack of subject-matter jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I part ways with the principal opinion only in its conclusion that the four licensing-offcial respondents are appropriate defendants under Ex parte Young."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thus, on that view, S. B. 8 permits the Medical Board to discipline physicians for violating the statute despite the Act's command that \u201cthe requirements of this subchapter shall be enforced exclusively through . . . private civil actions,\u201d \u201c [n]otwithstanding . . . any other law .\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5bfc2df3943f04277b26094114526ecbba2b7f2ed6dc8b51fdde62743965d4a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5bfc2df3943f-0004-0004",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Although some path to relief not recognized today may yet exist, the Court has now foreclosed the most straightforward route under its precedents."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
